{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal: adopt the web UI simplification design as the governing decision for the workroom UI. The design is the note at notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md with its interactive previews at notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification-preview.html, landed on main at merge a08c32f0 after independent review: two screens only — a single list of open requests, one sortable single-line row each (state, waits-on, age, title), priority order by default with click-to-sort on column headers and no prose ordering subheads; and a thread view whose railway stays but is drawn vertically alongside the spine rows, rendering by default only the salient acts that led to the current state, with history behind explicit expansion; no count anywhere without being one click from exactly its rows. Hugh directed the design on 2026-08-19, reviewed two preview rounds, and gave both refinements now incorporated; his earlier ratification attempt (9da1e7b4) targeted the commitment report and was correctly refused by the fold, so this proposal is the ratifiable adoption object. Ratification authorizes the implementation request, which planner files resting on the ratified decision; no source changes before that."}